===Glyph origin===
{{ja-etym-kokuji}}. According to ''Kanjigen'', an {{liushu|ic|nocap=1}}, superficially of {{affix|ja|nocat=1|木|万}} or {{m|ja|厉}}. According to Kōdansha's ''Shindaijiten'', {{unknown|ja|nocap=1}}, but raises a theory that it derives from a hypothetically earlier {{m|ja|櫔}} (simplifying 萬 → 万).

Speculative theory found elsewhere suggests a derivation from {{ja-r|栃木|とちぎ|{{w|Tochigi}}}}, the toponym with which the character is primarily associated: {{affix|ja|十|千|tr1=to|tr2=chi|t1=ten|t2=thousand}} is a [[yamato kotoba]] formulation of the number 10,000, also written as {{m|ja|万}} or {{m|ja|萬}},  whilst {{m|ja|木}} is read as ''ki'' or ''gi'', thus suggesting that the earlier form of the character be precisely an {{Han compound|ls=ic|木|萬|lang=ja|nocap=1}}, superficially aligning with ''Kanjigen''; however, the veracity of this is undetermined.

Additionally, assuming an origin in terms of {{affix|ja|nocat=1|木|萬}}, the addition of the upper {{m|ja|𠂆}} could be explained as an {{glossary|assimilation}} towards the similar characters {{m|ja|勵}} and {{m|ja|蠣}} (see spelling pronunciation below).

