===Etymology===
Seemingly related to {{cog|ojp|梅|tr=ume<sub>2</sub>}} (Shibatani, 1990; Miyake, 1997; apud {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007)}} (which was possibly borrowed from Middle Chinese). Its origin is unknown ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}); its [[referent]], {{taxfmt|Prunus mume|species}}, originated around the {{w|Yangtze River}},<ref name=uem>{{cite-journal|title=Phylogenetic relationships in the stone fruit group of ''Prunus'' as revealed by restriction fragment analysis of chloroplast DNA|journal=The Japanese Journal of Genetics|volume=66|year=1991|issue=1|page=60|text=''P. mume'' had its origin in South China around the Yangtze River (Kyotani, 1989b).|first=Chiyomi|last=Uematsu|first2=Tetsuo|last2=Sasakuma|first3=Yasunari|last3=Ogihara|doi=10.1266/jjg.66.59|pmid=1676591}}</ref> now in south China yet initially outside the {{w|Chinese civilization}}'s cradle in the {{w|Zhongyuan|Central Plain}}.

